- How would you adapt this to extract the odd bits instead of even bits?
- What are the trade-offs vs a loop-based approach on various architectures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of bitwise folding to compute parity without loops.

## Key Concepts
- Parity via XOR folding
- Bitwise shifts to mix bits
- No branches or loops in parity path

## Code Example
```javascript
uint32_t parity32(uint32_t n) {
  uint32_t p = n;
  p ^= p >> 16;
  p ^= p >> 8;
  p ^= p >> 4;
  p ^= p >> 2;
  p ^= p >> 1;
  return p & 1;
}
```

